.SH hee-cache-prune(1)
.PP
section: 1 hee-cache-prune -- prune stale entries from the real hee-*
disk caches (hee-filter\[aq]s repo-visibility cache, hee-git-merge\[aq]s
PR-detail cache).
A TTL alone never deletes an entry nobody re-queries -- it just sits
forever.
Real trigger: Spencer\[aq]s ask, 2026-08-24, \[dq]keep things clean\[dq]
-- meant to be cron\[aq]d via bootstrap.mk\[aq]s own
unprivileged-by-design mechanism
(\f[V]make -f tooling/bootstrap.mk install-cron\f[R]), not a one-off
manually-copied script.
.PP
Usage: hee-cache-prune [days, default 7]
.PP
